{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1235 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "b733227a220c8ce8651bd723692a834b23312cb8cfb6d8e4d069467335ace9c8" :edb/db-before-t 1234 :edb/db-after-t 1235 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534547 50 #inst "2026-10-07T22:07:46.528Z" 13194139534547 true] [17592186068697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294134 13194139534547 true] [17592186068697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294141 13194139534547 true] [17592186068697 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294148 13194139534547 true] [17592186068698 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294120 13194139534547 true] [17592186068698 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294127 13194139534547 true] [17592186294120 1017 #edb/ref 17592186294121 13194139534547 true] [17592186294120 1089 "q-121517" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294120 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534547 true] [17592186294120 1100 "Which integral gives the area of the finite region bounded between $y=8{x}^{2}-4$ and $y=2-2x?$" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294120 1113 #uuid "1495ffd4-708e-5569-a19d-b4ce8001edba" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294120 1145 "First, let's draw a sketch of the two functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/b2f34492ce184169d0e720d5a2214a356236b56d6e20bd8ece584b967f074e64.png)\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*\n\nNow, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-2x & =8{x}^{2}-4 \\\\ 8{x}^{2}+2x-6 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-2\\pm \\sqrt{{2}^{2}-4\\cdot 8\\cdot (-6)}}{2\\cdot 8} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm 14}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-1$ to $x=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, let's draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/94243d27b465eca7957731385b2fe13fae36b811079d3077e2e093aa19d81ad3.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=8{x}^{2}-4,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=2-2x.$\n\nTherefore, the integral that gives our area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}[\\,(2-2x)-(8{x}^{2}-4)\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}(-8{x}^{2}-2x+6)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294122 13194139534547 true] [17592186294121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294123 13194139534547 true] [17592186294121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294124 13194139534547 true] [17592186294121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294125 13194139534547 true] [17592186294121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294126 13194139534547 true] [17592186294121 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534547 true] [17592186294121 1041 "selection" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294121 1104 #edb/ref 17592186294126 13194139534547 true] [17592186294121 1110 #uuid "290f832c-5316-5e4e-8a45-7de3f3173b83" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294122 1034 "{\\int }_{-2}^{3/4}(-{x}^{2}+2x-6)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294122 1111 #uuid "d32a5dd5-a34f-5f2d-831e-7317b1b6e73b" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294123 1034 "{\\int }_{-1/4}^{3/4}(8{x}^{2}+x-3)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294123 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294123 1111 #uuid "e7a7e746-e6b3-50bb-b723-4f710817d632" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294124 1034 "{\\int }_{3/4}^{1}(-8{x}^{2}-3x+2)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294124 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294124 1111 #uuid "7ba6270e-1c65-5526-8e14-b85b0b7c39aa" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294125 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}(-4{x}^{2}-x+4)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294125 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294125 1111 #uuid "3dcb7b46-232a-586c-af00-748069ef18ca" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294126 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{3/4}(-8{x}^{2}-2x+6)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294126 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294126 1111 #uuid "fcdf8ae2-e353-5d35-97e1-4d825481885c" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294127 1017 #edb/ref 17592186294128 13194139534547 true] [17592186294127 1089 "q-121566" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294127 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534547 true] [17592186294127 1100 "Which integral gives the area of the finite region bounded by $y=2{x}^{2}-3x$ and $y=5-2{x}^{2}-2x?$" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294127 1113 #uuid "a08163fa-4d1f-55bf-a571-4e4e9630646e" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294127 1145 "First, let's draw a sketch of the two functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/9a4de823003f0461231c355a43ba9845358ec4a3767ca59c2ba2206456620373.png)\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*\n\nNow, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-3x & =5-2{x}^{2}-2x \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-x-5 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}-4\\cdot 4\\cdot (-5)}}{2\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-1$ to $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, let's draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/94b0113f7ca9ffeca11398cce06995fa4a7e5cb3f39b3021d5d6ec56746b75ee.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=2{x}^{2}-3x,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=5-2{x}^{2}-2x.$\n\nTherefore, the integral that gives our area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}[\\,(5-2{x}^{2}-2x)-(2{x}^{2}-3x)\\,]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}(-4{x}^{2}+x+5)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294129 13194139534547 true] [17592186294128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294130 13194139534547 true] [17592186294128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294131 13194139534547 true] [17592186294128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294132 13194139534547 true] [17592186294128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294133 13194139534547 true] [17592186294128 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534547 true] [17592186294128 1041 "selection" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294128 1104 #edb/ref 17592186294130 13194139534547 true] [17592186294128 1110 #uuid "b0f4d607-ef7b-5645-a072-8c0f866eed83" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294129 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{5/4}(-4{x}^{2}-x+5)\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294129 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294129 1111 #uuid "42551b9f-abde-5f3c-8eb6-5688a1c996a9" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294130 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}(-4{x}^{2}+x+5)\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294130 1111 #uuid "c63ecd13-53f8-5eb9-b484-f05af70dae96" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294131 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{4/5}(4{x}^{2}-x+5)\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294131 1111 #uuid "fa07377b-3bd3-5e51-bab3-af0a96068486" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294132 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{5/4}(4{x}^{2}-x-5)\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294132 1111 #uuid "75594be6-5839-5706-9bdf-2a9cf4607bf6" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294133 1034 "{\\int }_{-5/4}^{1}(4{x}^{2}+x-5)\\text{d}x" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534547 true] [17592186294133 1111 #uuid "73516eb3-9dc5-5773-819c-7d52696e0ae5" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294134 1017 #edb/ref 17592186294135 13194139534547 true] [17592186294134 1089 "q-121585" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294134 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534547 true] [17592186294134 1100 "Calculate the area of the finite region bounded by the curves $y=2{x}^{2}-2$ and $y=6.$" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294134 1113 #uuid "c84d87bd-9d44-56d4-92d0-f67ba8ac76ce" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294134 1145 "First, let's draw a sketch of the two functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/0fd8a89bdcad9f1b20c9fd35df9aa209a5e551d5d7a7c97f62103e23e7ae9741.png)\n\nNow, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-2 & =6 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-2$ to $x=2.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, we draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033713/assets/83e8d6af5284006b4caad6b1a96cb1298f7c7672d6c35fa652359d3a0b28e037.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=2{x}^{2}-2,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=6.$\n\nTherefore, we can find the area, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}[\\,(6)-(2{x}^{2}-2)\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}(8-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3})|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =[8\\cdot 2-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {2}^{3}]-[8\\cdot (-2)-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-2)^{3}] \\\\  & =(16-\\frac{16}{3})-(-16+\\frac{16}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534547 true] [17592186294135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294136 13194139534547 true] [17592186294135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294137 13194139534547 true] [17592186294135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294138 13194139534547 true] [17592186294135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294139 13194139534547 true] [1759218629